{
  "derivation_histories": {
    "dehanī": "The Mādhavīya explicitly glosses the feminine passively and invokes bāhulaka for lyuṭ in the patient sense, then gaurādi ṅīṣ.",
    "deha": "Mādhava analyses ghañ with the patient sense. Monier-Williams independently gives both m. and n.",
    "dehin": "ini in the possessive sense of 5.2.94 and 5.2.115. The masculine singular is dehī.",
    "dehalī": "Kṣīrasvāmin places it under Uṇādi and describes the wood below a door. Śabdakalpadruma instead gives deha + lā, ka at 3.2.3 and gaurādi ṅīṣ. Both explain the same lexical threshold."
  },
